scripts, configuration, tests, and developer documentation.

It does not apply to original editorial content: articles, tutorials, guides,
reviews, app descriptions, or their original illustrations and other media.
This includes content in src/content/, editorial text in src/pages/ and
src/data/, and copies or excerpts in generated indexes, feeds, or built pages.
See CONTENT-LICENSE for the copyright notice and terms for that material.
In files containing both software and editorial content, the respective
terms apply to each portion.

TechHut branding is also excluded from the software license. This includes
the TechHut and TechHut Media names, TECH/HUT wordmark, logos, favicons,
app icons, and other TechHut brand artwork, including branding embedded in
components or generated files. See BRANDING.md for the scope and terms.
Reusable implementation code remains BSD-licensed; the brand identity and
artwork it displays do not receive that license.

Third-party code, fonts, logos, images, quotations, and other materials retain
their own licenses and ownership. Preserve their existing notices; this
license does not replace those terms or grant rights to trademarks.

